  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Posting this here as Ron suggested it: \"If you feel strongly about an aspect of UDON or concerned about security or moderation aspect write it up in feedback.\"\nWith the power that Udon wields, we must all understand that some community members will exploit it. Udon won't always be used for good. This is why effective community moderation (and thusly effective moderators when ranked users report issues) is extremely important. I think those in staff that aren't working on the dev side of things really need to prioritize conceptualizing intelligent enforcement of 'bad eggs' so when devs are available, they are ready to act on tooling enforcement.\nThey don't need to do this alone. The community needs to be able to find/identify these bad eggs and moderators with the help of development staff need to create effective, understandable rules and tools to carry out enforcement. These tools need to be dynamic, prioritized for enforcement based on weights of the accused and the accuser[s] at the very least.\nThe \"Trusted\" rank is not a good tool to define who is actually trusted and not a good starting point for weights. It may be a meme at this point but \"Trusted users are more cancerous than new users in VRChat in 2019. Trusted is a synonym for untrustworthy.\"\nI believe that Community Labs was a good example of poor enforcement practices at VRChat. The moderators probably are doing their best, I can't see within the veil, but I don't believe they have the tools to properly carry out enforcement. 'Bad eggs' continue to post rule-breaking worlds, they are reported, they may be disciplined, who knows, but they come back later to continue with earnest.\nUdon has power to influence the VRChat experience moreso than anything VRChat has ever done, ever. Will it come in as a semi-rogue but extremely positive experience, or will it be something that cripples the communities trust of VRChat for a very long time? I would block a full-blown release until you have the tools to make sure this doesn't happen.",
